# Core runtime
APP_VERSION=0.4.0
DATA_DIR=./data
WHISPER_MODEL=small
WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu
WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE=int8

# Compatibility only: used by translation when no saved LLM provider exists.
# New LLM/TTS/remote-ASR provider credentials are stored in the database via
# Settings, not in this file. Do not put a production provider key in a URL.
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# The two local-ASR scene switches live in the database and default to true:
# material_transcription_use_local controls upload/material transcription;
# recording_evaluation_use_local controls learner-recording evaluation.
#
# Provider types are selected from the dynamic Settings catalog. Current core
# profiles include OpenAI/Responses/Azure OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, DeepSeek,
# Qwen/DashScope, Ollama, vLLM, MiMo, Azure Speech, Deepgram, and ElevenLabs.
#
# Endpoint conventions:
# - openai_audio_tts and openai_compatible_asr require a FULL user-provided
#   endpoint. The app never appends /audio/speech or /audio/transcriptions.
# - MiMo TTS/ASR use the FULL Chat Completions endpoint, commonly
#   https://api.xiaomimimo.com/v1/chat/completions.
# - Azure Speech, Deepgram, ElevenLabs, DashScope, and native OpenAI ASR
#   adapters take a base URL and add their documented resource path.
#
# The local-ASR switches above have independent effects:
# - material_transcription_use_local controls uploaded material segmentation
#   and needs a remote provider with transcribe + word_timestamps when off.
# - recording_evaluation_use_local controls learner recording evaluation and
#   needs only transcribe when off.
#
# See ../../PROVIDERS.md for the complete capability matrix and setup notes.
